TRIAGE SUMMARY, the tool-surface half of art:vscode-call-field-log-2026-10-05, 2026-10-05. Each item below was reproduced on reflow2 0.76.0 (what the work machine runs), then re-measured on 0.78.0 and on main at e7e304d, in scratch stores. The root-cause skill and the triage-feedback skill were fetched fresh. Main holds no tool-surface change after 0.78.0, so nothing here is "fixed on main only": every fix below ships in 0.78.0.

⭐ THE WORK MACHINE RUNS 0.76.0. Upgrade it to 0.78.0, or to 0.79.0 when released. Seventeen of the reporter's tool-surface frictions are gone on 0.78.0, two of them from entries written on 2026-10-05, two days after 0.78.0 shipped.

FIXED IN 0.78.0:
1. external_dependency with components as a string, refused naming neither tool nor field: #656 (chg:every-argument-refusal-names-the-tool-and-the-field-path). It is now "`external_dependency` … `components`: expected a list, each item a string", with the field's description, and every problem in one reply.
2. external_dependency replying with the TOML manifest instead of a receipt: #662 (chg:external-dependency-replies-with-a-receipt-and-a-re-declare-keeps-what-it-was-not-passed-2026-10-03). The reply is now the stored Resource.
3. find_tools not surfacing get_node: #659 (chg:get-node-reads-a-nodes-edges-2026-10-03). Measured ranks of get_node, 0.76.0 → 0.78.0:
   - "read one node by id with its properties and edges", 8th → 1st;
   - "list edges neighbours of a node", 9th → 1st;
   - "list edges of a node", 9th → 4th (inside the default 5).
4. get_node refusing include_edges (entries of 10-02 and 10-05): #659. It returns the node's edges with their properties.
5. add_change_event: affected, subject and rationale_basis each learned by a refusal: #656, one reply now lists all three with their shapes and values; #667 (chg:the-cli-describes-a-tool-with-its-schema-and-lessons-2026-10-03) shows them before the call (`reflow2-mcp --describe add_change_event`).
6. add_verification's verifies as a string, then as a list of strings: #656 names `verifies` and `verifies[0]` and says "expected an object with `target_id`"; #667 shows VerifyTargetReq.
7. add_verification's last_run_at without status: the refusal names set_verification_status on 0.76.0 already. The schema's "Refused without `status`" is now readable before the call (#667).
8. set_artifact_checksums missing disposition, "Its own schema publishes no description of it": #656 now quotes the description with design_holds, design_updated and baseline_established.
9. set_artifact_checksum's disposition guessed as design_change: the refusal names the three values on every version, and #667 shows them beforehand. The values are still prose, not an enum: see fact:a-value-set-published-without-an-enum-escapes-the-argument-check-so-every-one-is-listed-is-false-2026-10-05.
10. record_finding basis 'inferred' and confidence "high": #656, both in one reply; #667 shows the enum and the type. The missing home is still open: see fact:a-deferral-marker-and-a-code-read-observation-have-no-basis-and-the-default-says-measured-2026-10-05.
11. coverage_report given a list of strings: #656 names `observed[0]` and the {path} shape. The kind-2 URL half is still open: fact:coverage-report-still-claims-nothing-for-commit-pinned-url-locations-on-main-2026-10-05.
12. AUTHORED_BY role given prose: the enum was already published in tools/list on 0.76.0 but invisible through the door. #667 shows it, and #656 refuses before the tool runs.
13. add_decision related_to took four calls: two on 0.78.0. The first refusal lists all four problems (node_id with its nearest name other_id, the relation set, the missing evidence with its description).
14. Refused writes that left a node (the 10-01 [defect] and the 10-02 [defect?]): #655 (chg:a-refused-write-stores-nothing). Reproduced on 0.76.0: a refused add_requirement (provenance 'user') left the requirement at priority medium, and the reporter's third refused add_decision call left the decision. Neither is stored on 0.78.0. The "nothing moved" half is still open: fact:the-four-call-decision-was-a-leaked-node-and-an-edge-only-revise-still-says-nothing-moved-2026-10-05.
15. add_capability satisfies and allocated_to sent as lists: #656 names both fields ("expected a string, or null; got a list of 1"); #667 shows the type beforehand. That verifies takes a list of objects while satisfies takes one id is the recorded sibling-shape class (fact:defect-typed-tool-parameter-names-are-inconsistent), not new.
16. realizes conformance 'unverified': the enum was published on 0.76.0 but invisible through the door. #667 shows it; #656 refuses before the tool runs.
17. "Five writes each needed a refused attempt" (no up-front schemas): #667 (`--describe`, `--list-tools`, describe_schema with `tool`, and a `describe` pointer in every find_tools reply) and #656 (every argument problem in one reply). Four residual classes are recorded beside this summary; see below.

NOTHING TO FIX:
18. Requirement.priority 'should' in an import document: describe_schema {node_type: Requirement} served the enum on 0.76.0 already, and import_graph's own description points at it. The import refusal listed every bad item at once. The report's "serve the import/property schema" conclusion is overturned for this item.

STILL OPEN ON MAIN, one finding each, all with source art:vscode-call-field-log-2026-10-05:
- fact:external-dependency-stores-its-arguments-under-other-names-and-two-of-them-undeclared-2026-10-05;
- fact:create-time-fields-are-still-published-nowhere-and-the-describe-door-inherits-the-gap-2026-10-05 (add_epoch);
- fact:the-changeevent-description-decoy-is-listed-by-find-tools-and-passes-the-argument-check-2026-10-05;
- fact:a-deferral-marker-and-a-code-read-observation-have-no-basis-and-the-default-says-measured-2026-10-05;
- fact:coverage-report-still-claims-nothing-for-commit-pinned-url-locations-on-main-2026-10-05;
- fact:an-import-still-requires-component-purpose-where-add-component-takes-description-2026-10-05;
- fact:an-unknown-node-type-is-answered-with-the-known-types-only-by-create-node-2026-10-05;
- fact:a-value-set-published-without-an-enum-escapes-the-argument-check-so-every-one-is-listed-is-false-2026-10-05 (provenance 'user', disposition);
- fact:the-four-call-decision-was-a-leaked-node-and-an-edge-only-revise-still-says-nothing-moved-2026-10-05;
- fact:export-graph-with-no-arguments-still-prints-the-whole-design-on-main-2026-10-05;
- fact:a-constructors-revise-role-never-reaches-the-find-tools-summary-so-update-an-existing-node-misses-it-2026-10-05 (the 10-05 entry on marking an Artifact realized, appended the same day).

NOT ESTABLISHED: the reporter's own session logs were not available, so each item was reproduced from the words in the log, not replayed from the session. A measurement on these binaries says what THIS version does; that the reporter ran 0.76.0 comes from the log's Context section.
